  "scope": "R1 parser and internal arithmetic unchanged. External certificate revalidation for bounded integer comparisons only. Source strings are untrusted metadata; no source authenticity, web retrieval, signature validation or real theorem proof. No trust from a self-asserted verified flag.",
  "certificate": "Strict object with exactly method,claim,result. Method EXACT_INTEGER_COMPARISON; result JSON bool only; parse and bind to same canonical typed proposition (symmetric operand order and integer normalization, operator preserved); recompute result using pinned R1. Certificate validity is content verification, not issuer authentication. Symbolic certificates always rejected.",
  "reports": "Strict object claim,asserted_truth,source (bounded nonempty string). Bind canonical proposition with same operator; opposite operator reports not aggregated in R1.1. Count contradictory boolean reports as report_conflict, never as verified_evidence CONFLICT. All source metadata unauthenticated. Report and certificate list bounds 32 each, malformed envelope rejected; no promotion of truth.",
  "gate": "30/30 new controls and 20/20 baseline regression. Check expected status and counts, no source authentication claim or verified conflict; no external certificate alters R1 truth, no training/production/knowledge write. Same-author fixtures, no scientific generalization.",
